# SQL Data Cleaning Project

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates data-cleaning techniques
using PostgreSQL and SQL.

The objective was to transform raw customer data
into a standardized and analysis-ready dataset.

## Data Cleaning Tasks

- Identified and removed duplicate records
- Used CTEs and ROW_NUMBER()
- Removed leading and trailing spaces
- Standardized customer names
- Standardized gender values
- Standardized state abbreviations
- Converted emails to lowercase
- Cleaned phone-number formatting
- Handled NULL values
- Standardized date formats
- Performed data-quality validation

## SQL Concepts Used

- Common Table Expressions (CTEs)
- ROW_NUMBER()
- Window Functions
- CASE Statements
- GROUP BY
- HAVING
- COALESCE()
- TRIM()
- LOWER()
- UPPER()
- INITCAP()
- REGEXP_REPLACE()
- TO_DATE()
- UPDATE
- ALTER TABLE

## Tools

- PostgreSQL
- pgAdmin
- SQL
